<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">Two teams read a proposal and agree that a retry must be safe. They disagree about which component owns the stable key. Make the ownership and failure case concrete enough to review before implementation.</p>

<!-- @before Writing Discipline :: staff -->
### Describe one failure path precisely

Name the operation identity, who stores it and what the caller sees after a lost response. In the example below, a matching retry within the endpoint’s retention policy can replay the saved outcome. Record the final decision and its consequences once the review closes. [Documenting architecture decisions](https://cognitect.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions).
